#. translators: %s: Cloudflare dashboard URL.
#: admin/section-apo.php:34
#, php-format
msgid "Automatic Platform Optimization (APO) is an optional Cloudflare feature that caches the HTML of WordPress pages on the Cloudflare edge network using Cloudflare Workers. APO is enabled per zone in the Cloudflare dashboard under <a href=\"%s\">Speed → Optimization → Content</a>, it cannot be enabled or configured from this plugin."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: cf-edge-cache header name.
#: admin/section-apo.php:49
#, php-format
msgid "This plugin always sends the %s response header. Cloudflare uses this header to detect the WordPress integration (\"WordPress plugin successfully detected\" in the Cloudflare dashboard) and to decide whether the HTTP response may be cached by APO. The header has no effect when APO is not enabled for the zone."
msgstr ""

#: admin/section-apo.php:61
msgid "Request"
msgstr ""

#: admin/section-apo.php:62
msgid "Header"
msgstr ""

#: admin/section-apo.php:68
msgid "Anonymous visitor"
msgstr ""

#: admin/section-apo.php:73
msgid "Logged-in user"
msgstr ""

#: admin/section-apo.php:80
msgid "APO applies its own caching rules, which differ from the regular Cloudflare cache:"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: GET, 2: HEAD, 3: 200, 4: text/html.
#: admin/section-apo.php:90
#, php-format
msgid "Only %1$s and %2$s requests for HTML are cached, and only when the origin responds with status %3$s and content type %4$s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: utm_source, 2: fbclid, 3: gclid.
#: admin/section-apo.php:107
#, php-format
msgid "URLs with query parameters are not cached and are always fetched from the origin. The only exception is a fixed list of known marketing parameters, such as %1$s, %2$s and %3$s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: wp-, 2: woocommerce_.
#: admin/section-apo.php:123
#, php-format
msgid "Requests with cookies that start with certain prefixes, such as %1$s and %2$s, bypass the cache. Logged-in users and visitors with a shopping cart therefore always receive a fresh response from the origin."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: Cache-Control.
#: admin/section-apo.php:138
#, php-format
msgid "According to Cloudflare, APO ignores the origin %s header for edge caching and keeps pages in the edge cache for up to 30 days. The edge lifetimes from the \"Cache headers\" settings above therefore do not determine how long APO caches a page; the headers are still passed on to the browser."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: Cache Level: Bypass.
#: admin/section-apo.php:152
#, php-format
msgid "A Page Rule with %s that matches the request also disables APO for that request."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: cf-cache-status, 2: cf-apo-via, 3: cf-edge-cache.
#: admin/section-apo.php:168
#, php-format
msgid "To check whether a page is served by APO, inspect the response headers %1$s, %2$s and %3$s. The %2$s header also indicates why a request bypassed APO."
msgstr ""

